> Is there a way to "kill" a corpse so that there isn't a chance of
> revivication?

There's a chance a troll corpse will revive until the corpse is "old"
(which I think is 50 turns).  Ways to prevent this are:  level drain
the troll to level 0; throw the corpse in a pool/moat (doesn't work on
water trolls); polymorph/tin/eat the corpse, or get something else to
eat the corpse for you (pets, wandering gelatinous cubes, etc); lock
the corpse in a chest/large box.

There's probably others, but those are the ones I prefer.  Of course,
if you can easily kill a troll, you can sit around killing it over and
over, racking up experience and random objects.

